[{"id":2571499673,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6ZRfiZ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\nThe idea of having non-suspending breakpoints is a great one; finally I may no longer have to rely on `print()` statement debugging so much :slightly_smiling_face: \r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5ed934d9-150f-4de4-a2aa-d13d24ad8e06)\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- Using an unknown variable name (e.g. `counters >= 10` instead of `counter >= 10` in the above example) will fail silently. This should probably print an error when the line is first reached (but without breaking).\r\n- Using an unknown print name (e.g. `Value of counter: {counters}` instead of `Value of counter: {counter}`) won't replace the placeholder and no error is printed. I'd expect it to print an error (and leave the placeholder as-is).\r\n- Prints could make use of `print_line_rich()` instead of `print_line()` so you can use BBCode formatting within them. Right now, BBCode is printed as-is (`[color=red]{counter}[/color]` won't show up in red).\r\n- When a breakpoint has **Suspend Execution** disabled, it should have a different icon to distinguish it from breakpoints that don't suspend execution. This could be an outlined red circle, for instance. For conditional non-suspending breakpoints, the `=` sign could be present in red in the middle.\r\n- Since we have some space, we could rename **Suspend Execution** to **Suspend Execution if Condition is Met** just to be clear.\r\n- Changes are occasionally lost after I close and reopen the Edit Breakpoint dialog. It's inconsistent and I can't determine a pattern as to why it's occurring.\r\n- The error message that occurs when you use an invalid expression (I used `:` for my testing) isn't very clear. While the editor does point back to the script line where it occurred, it doesn't tell you that it's coming from an invalid conditional breakpoint. Ideally, it should do that, but also print the expression that was attempted to be parsed. (Printing the expression could also be done at the Expression class level.)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b321f669-d698-4a54-baa1-1be850a4cca8)\r\n\r\n> (I accidentally tried to use `||` instead of `or` for example).\r\n\r\nIt's strange that this is invalid in Expression, considering it's valid in GDScript (even if the preferred syntax is `or` as per the [style guide](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_styleguide.html)).\r\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100516#pullrequestreview-2571499673","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100516","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100516#pullrequestreview-2571499673"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100516"}},"submitted_at":"2025-01-24T02:11:46Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2845454628,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6pmjEk","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?u=f0c85fe8c24debe91dc14d7efa97b51a19250b47&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Seems to work well.\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\nThe hover breakpoint color is too dark on dark theme:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89bb3a1b-dbad-48e3-98ea-5f9995cd0fa3)\r\n\r\nThe breakpoints panel in the debugger should use the same icons and colors as in the script.\r\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100516#pullrequestreview-2845454628","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100516","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100516#pullrequestreview-2845454628"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100516"}},"submitted_at":"2025-05-27T16:35:13Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2872472063,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6rNnH_","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?u=52abfc655fe5217a9500bfc7d8276c59a069d259&v=4","gravatar_